# Feature-liveness watchdog state.  Runtime output like every entry above, but
# it was the one that got committed — the sole tracked file under data/ — so
# every local `pytest` run rewrote it and left the tree dirty on a
# timestamp-only diff.  That trains reviewers to wave through changes to the
# file whose whole job is to page when a measurement flat-lines.  Production
# reads it from the 360scalp-v2-data volume, the writer recreates it
# (`makedirs` + atomic replace), and monitor_heartbeat treats "missing" as a
# pre-rollout build, so nothing needs it in the checkout.  `.tmp` sibling
# ignored for the same reason data/pricing_freshness.json.tmp is.
data/feature_liveness.json
# Live SAR mechanism arms (src/sar_live_shadow.py). Runtime output: the engine
# rewrites it on a 60s heartbeat, and any test that exercises TradeMonitor's
# poll writes it too — which is how it briefly got tracked (2026-07-30).
data/sar_live_arms_v1.json
data/sar_live_arms_v1.json.tmp
data/feature_liveness.json
# Live SAR mechanism arms (src/sar_live_shadow.py). Runtime output: the engine
# rewrites it on a 60s heartbeat, and any test that exercises TradeMonitor's
# poll writes it too — which is how it briefly got tracked (2026-07-30).
data/sar_live_arms_v1.json
data/sar_live_arms_v1.json.tmp.tmp

# Stray atomic-write sibling from an in-memory ledger (`path=""`) — the
# ledgers now short-circuit before writing it, and it must never be committed
# again: it differs on every branch and conflicted on every merge.
.tmp
